From 9f6393b0ef284f2a4fc79f0e355094984b8f7d0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/24] Revert "ARM: gts28ltexx: enable the DECON System MMUs"

This reverts commit c7dbdcf2f.

With the DECON System MMUs on, importing a panfrost dma-buf into
exynos-drm succeeds, and Hyprland 0.57 keeps the imports of client
buffers alive after their surfaces are gone: every shell panel opened
and closed left about 10 MB attached to DECON.  On arm32 exynos-drm
maps imports into a fixed 1 GiB IOVA window (exynos_drm_dma.c:30-31);
once about 1 GB was held, new imports failed, Hyprland rejected the
shell's buffers and the shell crash-looped (black screen), twice.

Without the System MMU only physically contiguous buffers can be
imported, so the same leak grows about ten times slower (+67 MB of
Shmem for 5 drawer openings instead of +344 MB) and the shell keeps
working.  Turn the System MMUs back off until the userland leak is
fixed; the Omarchy image keeps its dmabuf-check shim meanwhile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
